  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.26 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.46. The FLUX.2 Klein picture edit completes on slower GPUs in the browser (an RX 590 in Chrome lost the device on 5.8.25; the transformer now ends a command buffer after every block). Compiler caches are freed once per model after its warm-up (CompilerCachePolicy, on by default for WebGPU / WebGL / Wasm): a disposed model no longer leaves 6.5-16 MiB of compiler state on the browser heap, and with SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.46 a model loaded again compiles nothing in the browser. Apps that assemble a model from components call CompilerCachePolicy.ModelWarmedUp(accelerator) once after its first complete run. Streaming model loads survive a transient connection reset (the models host is retried once before falling back to Hugging Face; one reset used to make a 0.5 GB load 3x slower). SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.46: deterministic WGSL / GLSL, the shader artifact cache on Wasm and WebGL, WebGL buffers tiled to MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE.",
